{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Standalone loudness analyzer for post-production in REAPER. Horizontal timeline UI with M/S/I curves, target line, heatmap, grid, and source comparison (Dialog/Master).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A custom JSFX audio plugin that simulates the fluttering sound of butterfly wings. It uses a combination of LFOs, noise, and filters to create a dynamic and evolving soundscape that captures the delicate and chaotic nature of butterfly flight. Perfect for adding an organic, natural element to your music or sound design projects. Flap Speed Control: Adjust the frequency of the wing flaps, allowing for slow, gentle fluttering or rapid, frantic movement. Wing Sharpness: Control the shape of the flap envelope, from soft and rounded to sharp and percussive, to mimic different butterfly species or flight styles. Air Resonance: A resonant filter that simulates the natural frequencies of air around the wings, adding a sense of space and realism to the sound. Turbulence Control: Add high-frequency noise to simulate the chaotic air movement caused by the wings, with a mix control to blend it in with the main sound. Wing Air Push: A low-frequency component that simulates the powerful push of air generated by the wings, adding depth and weight to the sound. Stereo Width: Control the stereo spread of the sound, from mono to wide, to create a more immersive and dynamic soundscape. Flight Chaos: An LFO that adds random modulation to the flap speed and turbulence, simulating the unpredictable nature of butterfly flight. Inertia & Swarm Behavior: Smooth parameter transitions and a chaos LFO that creates a sense of inertia and swarm-like movement, making the sound feel alive and evolving over time. The plugin also includes a play switch and a start/stop ramp for smooth transitions in and out of the sound.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 5.1 Follower that pans audio to follow Phantom Center position from SBP Surround Scope. Includes coordinate transformation (offset, scale, invert) and pseudo-acoustic filtering based on angle difference. Link slider1/2 to SurroundScope slider24/25 via Parameter Modulation.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 5.1 Surround Sound Field Analyzer with heat map, phase correlation, and level meters. Monitoring-only: audio passes through unmodified. Visualises energy distribution i[...]
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This script provides an advanced chord voicing editor for MIDI within REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab ADD CHORD (Triads, Sus, Dim, Aug)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab ADD INTERVAL (Extensions)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab CHORD VOICING (Inversions, Drops, Voice Leading + Glue)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab SELECTION (Select All + Filter)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab TOOLS (Octaves, Duplication, Glue)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 6.\tx360\tab HUMANIZE (Classic Buttons + Sliders)\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Physically-modeled engine sound synthesizer combining pulse-train excitation, waveguide exhaust resonance, filtered noise layers, and turbo. Features real firing orders and dual RPM control modes.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 SBP MotorSynth UI\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Automotive cockpit controller for SBP MotorSynth JSFX. Dual-gauge cockpit (tachometer + speedometer), vertical gear strip, interactive pedals, and tabbed parameter panels.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MotorSynth 2 is a procedural vehicle sound instrument with a WebUI, spatial listening positions, vehicle presets and multichannel stems. Eight vehicle profiles; modular engine, exhaust, road, cabin and electric sounds; 3D listener placement; Doppler pass-bys and 32-channel stems. Optional physical engine: the EngineSim Stems CLAP (separate download for Windows, macOS and Linux) plays real engine-sim .mr profiles in sync. Optional BOOM GRIP road and tyre layer (requires its own licence). Interfaces are available in English, Ukrainian and Simplified Chinese. Requires REAPER, ReaImGui and ReaWebAPI 0.3.9.10 or newer. Open the Control Center action to create a vehicle, prepare routing and record. MotorSynth 2 installs separately from the original MotorSynth.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 SBP ReaMotion Pad\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A powerful modulation and automation workstation for REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Features:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Vector Pad for morphing between 4 parameter states.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Master LFO and MSEG modulators with cross-modulation (FM/AM).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Independent Modulator with 7 mixing modes (Individual, Add, Multiply, Subtract, Min, Max, Power).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Real-time modulation preview and recording (Bake to automation items).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Advanced LFO parameters: Rate Sweep, Depth Ramp, and Random Steps.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Integrated preset system and state randomization.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr?cmd=_donations&business=bodzik@gmail.com&item_name=ReaMotionPad+Support&currency_code=USD"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
{\b Donate / Support}
}}}
\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 SBP ReaMotionPad Mixer\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 An auxiliary mixer effect designed for use with the ReaMotion Pad script. Summates up to 4 multichannel sources (up to 16 channels each) into a stereo output. Supports independent gain automation for each source and master level.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr?cmd=_donations&business=bodzik@gmail.com&item_name=ReaMotionPad+Support&currency_code=USD"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
{\b Donate / Support}
}}}
\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 SBP ReaSciFi\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Modular sci-fi UI sound generator for REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Features in this initial implementation:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Dedicated JSFX preview engine for one-shot and drone design.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Macro workflow for UI beeps, clicks, glitches, drones, and telemetry textures.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Timbre and Motion XY pads.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Built-in LFO and MSEG-style modulation controls.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Factory preset families oriented toward interface sound design.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.paypal.com/cgi-bin/webscr?cmd=_donations&business=bodzik@gmail.com&item_name=ReaSciFi+Support&currency_code=USD"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
{\b Donate / Support}
}}}
\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Starter JSFX engine for SBP ReaSciFi. Hybrid one-shot/drone preview generator with digital, packet, noise, resonator and Chua-inspired layers.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A transient-triggered particle tail for SBP ReaWhoosh. One peak launches a decaying stream of independent grains: it is not a repeated delay line. The display is a spatial map, not a decoration.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 granular tail fx for SBP_ReaWhoosh\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 SBP QuantumDress\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A multiband spectral motion delay for REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab 4\u8211-24 independently delayed spectral bands\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Editable five-point spectrum-to-delay curve with per-point LFO movement\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Cross-band feedback, transient scatter, spectral drift and dispersion\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Spectral stereo spread, macro controls, tempo sync and output safety\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Start with low feedback, then shape movement with the curve and macros.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaWhoosh is a tool for automatically creating whoosh-type sound effects.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Implementation of chain of effects (UltraComb) represent by AU5 Parallel Comb / Disperser / Shift core -> reorderable creative modules\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creative stereo sound-design processor inspired by AU5's parallel-delay comb. Comb / Disperser / Frequency Shift core with reorderable creative modules, two assignable LFOs, Envelope/ADR sources, Morph/Randomize and live spectrograms. WebUI requires ReaWebAPI 0.3.9.10 or newer, installed separately, then a REAPER restart. Import https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/master/index.xml in ReaPack and install "ReaWebAPI: Web Runtime for REAPER". Keep the complete package directory together. UltraComb 2.40 is not replaced.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 At the edit cursor, analyzes either a CutScene item or an SFX EVENT/PROCESS/ DESIGN marker, using frames from the configured source-video track.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 AI-assisted SFX spotting tool for REAPER. Analyzes video frames with local Ollama, displays copyable UCS-style tags, and generates SFX through MMAudio or StableDaw.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Builds configurable multi-output VSTi track structures and routing in REAPER. Supports same-track, legacy split, MIDI-only and output-only routing schemes, MIDI channels or buses, presets, folders and multiple send modes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires REAPER 7.0 or newer and the ReaImGui extension.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Select a destination track and a region in the source ruler lane. Copies ALL regions in that lane to empty items with the same bounds, text (item notes) and color. Original regions are preserved. If the source is ambiguous, a menu lists all lanes containing regions. Requires the native GetRegionOrMarker API; no extensions required.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates one region spanning from the earliest start to the latest end of all selected media items. The region is named automatically using the next available episode number: Ep1, Ep2, Ep3, etc.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Uses the active takes of the currently selected items as references. Selects every project item whose active take points to any of the same underlying audio files. Source sections and reversed sources are resolved to their root source. MIDI and empty items are ignored.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Assign Shift+Q to this action in REAPER. The open VO Tool consumes the request and performs alignment using its current settings.\par}
}
